+# Changelog
+
+## 3.5.0
+
+- New option `flush_interval_ms`: the worker flushes the output after this interval instead of after each message. The default 0 keeps the old behavior.
+- New function `engine_set_option()` changes `log_level`, `queue_depth`, or `flush_interval_ms` of a running engine.
+- New function `engine_version()` returns the version string of the engine.
+- `engine_create()` refuses more than 64 worker threads.
+
+## 3.4.0
+
+- `engine_submit()` returns `ENGINE_ESTATE` when the queue is full.
+- Messages larger than 1 MiB are refused with `ENGINE_EINVAL`.
